{"id":"mahabharata-6-112","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":112,"title":"द्वादशाधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 112 · Tenth day: Bhishma's great battle","summary":{"en":"Abhimanyu, Bhima and the Pandava heroes tear into the Kaurava army while Bhishma shines under his palm banner. As Shikhandin comes at him, Bhishma withdraws his weapon, and Arjuna slaughters the Kauravas after confusing the grandsire.","kn":"ಅಭಿಮನ್ಯು, ಭೀಮ ಮತ್ತಿತರ ಪಾಂಡವ ವೀರರು ಕೌರವ ಸೈನ್ಯವನ್ನು ಹರಿಯುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಭೀಷ್ಮ ತಾಳೆಧ್ವಜದಡಿ ಪ್ರಕಾಶಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಶಿಖಂಡಿ ಎದುರಾದಾಗ ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಆಯುಧ ಹಿಂತೆಗೆಯುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅರ್ಜುನ ಪಿತಾಮಹನನ್ನು ಗೊಂದಲಗೊಳಿಸಿ ಕೌರವರನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"अभिमन्यु, भीम और अन्य पाण्डव वीर कौरव सेना को चीरते हैं और भीष्म ताड़ध्वज के नीचे दमकते हैं। शिखण्डी के सामने आने पर भीष्म अस्त्र रोक लेते हैं, और अर्जुन पितामह को उलझाकर कौरवों का संहार करते हैं।","te":"అభిమన్యుడు, భీముడు, ఇతర పాండవ వీరులు కౌరవసేనను చీల్చుతారు; భీష్ముడు తాళధ్వజం కింద ప్రకాశిస్తాడు. శిఖండి ఎదురైనప్పుడు భీష్ముడు అస్త్రాన్ని ఉపసంహరిస్తాడు; అర్జునుడు పితామహుని కలవరపరచి కౌరవులను చంపుతాడు.","ta":"அபிமன்யு, பீமன் மற்றும் பாண்டவ வீரர்கள் கௌரவப் படையைக் கிழிக்க, பீஷ்மர் பனைக்கொடியின் கீழ் ஒளிர்கிறார். சிகண்டி எதிரே வர பீஷ்மர் ஆயுதத்தை விலக்குகிறார்; அர்ஜுனன் பிதாமகரைக் குழப்பிக் கௌரவரை அழிக்கிறான்.","ml":"പുലർകാലത്ത് ഭീഷ്മർ പനക്കൊടിക്കീഴിൽ തിളങ്ങുമ്പോൾ അഭിമന്യുവും ഭീമനും പാണ്ഡവ വീരന്മാരും കൗരവ സേനയെ ഛിന്നഭിന്നമാക്കുന്നു. ശിഖണ്ഡി അടുത്തെത്തിയപ്പോൾ ഭീഷ്മർ ആയുധം പിൻവലിക്കുന്നു; പിതാമഹനെ കുഴപ്പിച്ചശേഷം അർജുനൻ കൗരവരെ കൂട്ടക്കൊല ചെയ്യുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.112; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अभिमन्युर्महाराज तव पुत्रमयोधयत् ।\nमहत्या सेनया युक्तो भीष्महेतोः पराक्रमी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Abhimanyu, great king, fought your son Duryodhana, the valiant warrior leading a great army for Bhishma's sake."}},{"n":2,"text":"दुर्योधनो रणे कार्ष्णिं नवभिर्नतपर्वभिः ।\nआजघान रणे क्रुद्धः पुनश्चैनं त्रिभिः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana, angry, struck Subhadra's son in the battle with nine smooth-jointed arrows, and then again with three."}},{"n":3,"text":"तस्य शक्तिं रणे कार्ष्णिर्मृत्योर्घोरामिव स्वसाम् ।\nप्रेषयामास संक्रुद्धो दुर्योधनरथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Abhimanyu, enraged, hurled at Duryodhana's chariot a spear as dreadful as Death's own sister."}},{"n":4,"text":"तामापतन्तीं सहसा घोररूपां विशां पते ।\nद्विधा चिच्छेद ते पुत्रः क्षुरप्रेण महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"O lord of the people, your son, the great warrior, cut that terrible spear in two with a razor-headed arrow as it suddenly flew at him."}},{"n":5,"text":"तां शक्तिं पतितां दृष्ट्वा कार्ष्णिः परमकोपनः ।\nदुर्योधनं त्रिभिर्बाणैर्बाह्वोरुरसि चार्पयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the spear fallen, Abhimanyu, extremely angry, struck Duryodhana in the arms and chest with three arrows."}},{"n":6,"text":"पुनश्चैनं शरैर्घोरैराजघान स्तनान्तरे ।\nदशभिर्भरतश्रेष्ठ दुर्योधनममर्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, best of the Bharatas, he struck the furious Duryodhana again between the breasts with ten dreadful arrows."}},{"n":7,"text":"तद्युद्धमभवद्घोरं चित्ररूपं च भारत ।\nईक्षितृप्रीतिजननं सर्वपार्थिवपूजितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That battle was fearsome and wonderful, O Bharata, a delight to watch and praised by all the kings."}},{"n":8,"text":"भीष्मस्य निधनार्थाय पार्थस्य विजयाय च ।\nयुयुधाते रणे वीरौ सौभद्रकुरुपुंगवौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"For Bhishma's death and for Arjuna's victory, the two heroes, Subhadra's son and the bull of the Kurus, fought in the battle."}},{"n":9,"text":"सात्यकिं रभसं युद्धे द्रौणिर्ब्राह्मणपुंगवः ।\nआजघानोरसि क्रुद्धो नाराचेन परंतपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona's son Ashvatthama, the foremost brahmin, angrily struck the impetuous Satyaki in the chest with an iron arrow in the fight."}},{"n":10,"text":"शैनेयोऽपि गुरोः पुत्रं सर्वमर्मसु भारत ।\nअताडयदमेयात्मा नवभिः कङ्कपत्रिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki, of measureless spirit, in turn struck his teacher's son in all his vital spots with nine heron-feathered arrows, O Bharata."}},{"n":11,"text":"अश्वत्थामा तु समरे सात्यकिं नवभिः शरैः ।\nत्रिंशता च पुनस्तूर्णं बाह्वोरुरसि चार्पयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Ashvatthama quickly wounded Satyaki in the arms and chest with nine arrows and then thirty."}},{"n":12,"text":"सोऽतिविद्धो महेष्वासो द्रोणपुत्रेण सात्वतः ।\nद्रोणपुत्रं त्रिभिर्बाणैराजघान महायशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though badly hurt by Drona's son, the renowned archer of the Satvata line struck Drona's son with three arrows."}},{"n":13,"text":"पौरवो धृष्टकेतुं च शरैरासाद्य संयुगे ।\nबहुधा दारयां चक्रे महेष्वासं महारथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Paurava met Dhrishtaketu in the battle and wounded that great archer and great warrior in many places with arrows."}},{"n":14,"text":"तथैव पौरवं युद्धे धृष्टकेतुर्महारथः ।\nत्रिंशता निशितैर्बाणैर्विव्याध सुमहाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise the mighty great warrior Dhrishtaketu pierced the Paurava with thirty sharp arrows."}},{"n":15,"text":"पौरवस्तु धनुश्छित्त्वा धृष्टकेतोर्महारथः ।\nननाद बलवन्नादं विव्याध दशभिः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Paurava great warrior, having cut Dhrishtaketu's bow, roared mightily and struck him with ten arrows."}},{"n":16,"text":"सोऽन्यत्कार्मुकमादाय पौरवं निशितैः शरैः ।\nआजघान महाराज त्रिसप्तत्या शिलीमुखैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking another bow, Dhrishtaketu struck the Paurava, great king, with seventy-three sharp arrows."}},{"n":17,"text":"तौ तु तत्र महेष्वासौ महामात्रौ महारथौ ।\nमहता शरवर्षेण परस्परमवर्षताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the two great archers, great warriors and great-spirited, rained huge showers of arrows on each other."}},{"n":18,"text":"अन्योन्यस्य धनुश्छित्त्वा हयान्हत्वा च भारत ।\nविरथावसियुद्धाय संगतौ तौ महारथौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Each cut the other's bow and killed his horses, O Bharata, and, now without chariots, the two great warriors came together for a sword fight."}},{"n":19,"text":"आर्षभे चर्मणी चित्रे शतचन्द्रपरिष्कृते ।\nतारकाशतचित्रौ च निस्त्रिंशौ सुमहाप्रभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"They took up bright shields of bull-hide, adorned with a hundred moons and spangled with hundreds of stars, and gleaming swords of great brilliance."}},{"n":20,"text":"प्रगृह्य विमलौ राजंस्तावन्योन्यमभिद्रुतौ ।\nवाशितासंगमे यत्तौ सिंहाविव महावने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking up those spotless swords, king, they rushed at each other like two lions in a great forest at the meeting of the seasons for mating."}},{"n":21,"text":"मण्डलानि विचित्राणि गतप्रत्यागतानि च ।\nचेरतुर्दर्शयन्तौ च प्रार्थयन्तौ परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They moved in wonderful circles, advancing and retreating, displaying their skill and each looking for an opening."}},{"n":22,"text":"पौरवो धृष्टकेतुं तु शङ्खदेशे महासिना ।\nताडयामास संक्रुद्धस्तिष्ठ तिष्ठेति चाब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Paurava angrily struck Dhrishtaketu with his great sword on the temple, saying, \"Stand, stand!\""}},{"n":23,"text":"चेदिराजोऽपि समरे पौरवं पुरुषर्षभम् ।\nआजघान शिताग्रेण जत्रुदेशे महासिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king of the Chedis, in turn, struck the noble Paurava on the collarbone with the sharp point of his great sword."}},{"n":24,"text":"तावन्योन्यं महाराज समासाद्य महाहवे ।\nअन्योन्यवेगाभिहतौ निपेततुररिंदमौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Colliding in that great battle, O great king, the two scourges of enemies fell, each struck down by the other's force."}},{"n":25,"text":"ततः स्वरथमारोप्य पौरवं तनयस्तव ।\nजयत्सेनो रथे राजन्नपोवाह रणाजिरात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then your son Jayatsena lifted the Paurava onto his own chariot and carried him from the battlefield, king."}},{"n":26,"text":"धृष्टकेतुं च समरे माद्रीपुत्रः परंतपः ।\nअपोवाह रणे राजन्सहदेवः प्रतापवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the mighty Sahadeva, son of Madri, scourge of foes, carried Dhrishtaketu away from the fight, O king."}},{"n":27,"text":"चित्रसेनः सुशर्माणं विद्ध्वा नवभिराशुगैः ।\nपुनर्विव्याध तं षष्ट्या पुनश्च नवभिः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chitrasena wounded Susharma with nine swift arrows, and again with sixty, and again with nine."}},{"n":28,"text":"सुशर्मा तु रणे क्रुद्धस्तव पुत्रं विशां पते ।\nदशभिर्दशभिश्चैव विव्याध निशितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Susharma, enraged, wounded your son, lord of the people, with ten sharp arrows, and ten again."}},{"n":29,"text":"चित्रसेनश्च तं राजंस्त्रिंशता नतपर्वणाम् ।\nआजघान रणे क्रुद्धः स च तं प्रत्यविध्यत ।\nभीष्मस्य समरे राजन्यशो मानं च वर्धयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chitrasena in anger struck him with thirty smooth-jointed arrows, and Susharma wounded him back, both increasing Bhishma's fame and honor in the war, O king."}},{"n":30,"text":"सौभद्रो राजपुत्रं तु बृहद्बलमयोधयत् ।\nआर्जुनिं कोसलेन्द्रस्तु विद्ध्वा पञ्चभिरायसैः ।\nपुनर्विव्याध विंशत्या शरैः संनतपर्वभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Abhimanyu fought the prince Brihadbala. The king of Kosala struck Arjuna's son with five iron arrows and then again with twenty smooth-jointed arrows."}},{"n":31,"text":"बृहद्बलं च सौभद्रो विद्ध्वा नवभिरायसैः ।\nनाकम्पयत संग्रामे विव्याध च पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Abhimanyu wounded Brihadbala with nine iron arrows but did not shake him in the battle, and wounded him again and again."}},{"n":32,"text":"कौसल्यस्य पुनश्चापि धनुश्चिच्छेद फाल्गुणिः ।\nआजघान शरैश्चैव त्रिंशता कङ्कपत्रिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Phalguna's son cut the Kosala prince's bow again and struck him with thirty heron-feathered arrows."}},{"n":33,"text":"सोऽन्यत्कार्मुकमादाय राजपुत्रो बृहद्बलः ।\nफाल्गुनिं समरे क्रुद्धो विव्याध बहुभिः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking another bow, the prince Brihadbala, angry in the fight, wounded Arjuna's son with many arrows."}},{"n":34,"text":"तयोर्युद्धं समभवद्भीष्महेतोः परंतप ।\nसंरब्धयोर्महाराज समरे चित्रयोधिनोः ।\nयथा देवासुरे युद्धे मयवासवयोरभूत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their fight, scourge of enemies, took place for Bhishma's sake: two enraged warriors of marvelous skill, like the battle of Maya and Indra in the war of gods and demons."}},{"n":35,"text":"भीमसेनो गजानीकं योधयन्बह्वशोभत ।\nयथा शक्रो वज्रपाणिर्दारयन्पर्वतोत्तमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena looked magnificent as he fought the elephant division, like thunderbolt-wielding Indra splitting the greatest mountains."}},{"n":36,"text":"ते वध्यमाना भीमेन मातङ्गा गिरिसंनिभाः ।\nनिपेतुरुर्व्यां सहिता नादयन्तो वसुंधराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck down by Bhima, those elephants, like mountains, fell together on the earth and made it resound."}},{"n":37,"text":"गिरिमात्रा हि ते नागा भिन्नाञ्जनचयोपमाः ।\nविरेजुर्वसुधां प्राप्य विकीर्णा इव पर्वताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mountain-sized elephants, like heaps of crushed collyrium, lay scattered on the ground like shattered mountains."}},{"n":38,"text":"युधिष्ठिरो महेष्वासो मद्रराजानमाहवे ।\nमहत्या सेनया गुप्तं पीडयामास संगतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great archer Yudhishthira attacked the king of Madra, who was protected by a large army, and pressed him hard in the fight."}},{"n":39,"text":"मद्रेश्वरश्च समरे धर्मपुत्रं महारथम् ।\nपीडयामास संरब्धो भीष्महेतोः पराक्रमी ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the king of Madra, the valiant, angrily pressed the great warrior, son of Dharma, for Bhishma's sake."}},{"n":40,"text":"विराटं सैन्धवो राजा विद्ध्वा संनतपर्वभिः ।\nनवभिः सायकैस्तीक्ष्णैस्त्रिंशता पुनरर्दयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Sindhu king struck Virata with smooth-jointed arrows, then with nine sharp arrows and again with thirty, tormenting him."}},{"n":41,"text":"विराटश्च महाराज सैन्धवं वाहिनीमुखे ।\nत्रिंशता निशितैर्बाणैराजघान स्तनान्तरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Virata, great king, struck the Sindhu king between the breasts with thirty sharp arrows at the front of the army."}},{"n":42,"text":"चित्रकार्मुकनिस्त्रिंशौ चित्रवर्मायुधध्वजौ ।\nरेजतुश्चित्ररूपौ तौ संग्रामे मत्स्यसैन्धवौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"With their wonderful bows and swords, and their wonderful armor, weapons and banners, the Matsya and the Sindhu king shone marvelously in the battle."}},{"n":43,"text":"द्रोणः पाञ्चालपुत्रेण समागम्य महारणे ।\nमहासमुदयं चक्रे शरैः संनतपर्वभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona, meeting the son of Prishata Drupada, in the great battle made a huge heap of smooth-jointed arrows."}},{"n":44,"text":"ततो द्रोणो महाराज पार्षतस्य महद्धनुः ।\nछित्त्वा पञ्चाशतेषूणां पार्षतं समविध्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, great king, Drona cut the great bow of Dhrishtadyumna and wounded him with fifty arrows."}},{"n":45,"text":"सोऽन्यत्कार्मुकमादाय पार्षतः परवीरहा ।\nद्रोणस्य मिषतो युद्धे प्रेषयामास सायकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking another bow, Dhrishtadyumna, killer of enemy heroes, loosed arrows at Drona as he watched in the fight."}},{"n":46,"text":"ताञ्शराञ्शरसंघैस्तु संनिवार्य महारथः ।\nद्रोणो द्रुपदपुत्राय प्राहिणोत्पञ्च सायकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great warrior Drona, turning those arrows aside with volleys of his own, sent five arrows at the son of Drupada."}},{"n":47,"text":"तस्य क्रुद्धो महाराज पार्षतः परवीरहा ।\nद्रोणाय चिक्षेप गदां यमदण्डोपमां रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Furious, great king, Dhrishtadyumna, slayer of enemy heroes, hurled at Drona a mace like Yama's rod."}},{"n":48,"text":"तामापतन्तीं सहसा हेमपट्टविभूषिताम् ।\nशरैः पञ्चाशता द्रोणो वारयामास संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"As it suddenly flew at him, adorned with golden plates, Drona turned it aside in the battle with fifty arrows."}},{"n":49,"text":"सा छिन्ना बहुधा राजन्द्रोणचापच्युतैः शरैः ।\nचूर्णीकृता विशीर्यन्ती पपात वसुधातले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cut to pieces by the arrows loosed from Drona's bow, the mace was ground to powder and fell scattering to the earth, king."}},{"n":50,"text":"गदां विनिहतां दृष्ट्वा पार्षतः शत्रुसूदनः ।\nद्रोणाय शक्तिं चिक्षेप सर्वपारशवीं शुभाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his mace destroyed, Dhrishtadyumna, destroyer of foes, hurled at Drona a lovely iron spear."}},{"n":51,"text":"तां द्रोणो नवभिर्बाणैश्चिच्छेद युधि भारत ।\nपार्षतं च महेष्वासं पीडयामास संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona cut it in the fight with nine arrows, Bharata, and wounded the great archer, Prishata's son."}},{"n":52,"text":"एवमेतन्महद्युद्धं द्रोणपार्षतयोरभूत् ।\nभीष्मं प्रति महाराज घोररूपं भयानकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So this great and terrible battle of Drona and Dhrishtadyumna went on, great king, directed against Bhishma."}},{"n":53,"text":"अर्जुनः प्राप्य गाङ्गेयं पीडयन्निशितैः शरैः ।\nअभ्यद्रवत संयत्तं वने मत्तमिव द्विपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna, reaching the son of Ganga and wounding him with sharp arrows, charged at him as he stood ready, as against a rutting elephant in a forest."}},{"n":54,"text":"प्रत्युद्ययौ च तं पार्थं भगदत्तः प्रतापवान् ।\nत्रिधा भिन्नेन नागेन मदान्धेन महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But the mighty and glorious Bhagadatta came out against the son of Pritha, on an elephant gushing rut in three streams and blinded by its frenzy."}},{"n":55,"text":"तमापतन्तं सहसा महेन्द्रगजसंनिभम् ।\nपरं यत्नं समास्थाय बीभत्सुः प्रत्यपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that elephant, like Indra's own Airavata, suddenly charged, Bibhatsu faced it, making a supreme effort."}},{"n":56,"text":"ततो गजगतो राजा भगदत्तः प्रतापवान् ।\nअर्जुनं शरवर्षेण वारयामास संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the glorious king Bhagadatta, riding his elephant, held Arjuna off with a shower of arrows in the battle."}},{"n":57,"text":"अर्जुनस्तु रणे नागमायान्तं रजतोपमम् ।\nविमलैरायसैस्तीक्ष्णैरविध्यत महारणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna in turn struck the elephant, white-like-silver, as it advanced, with sharp, spotless iron arrows in that great fight."}},{"n":58,"text":"शिखण्डिनं च कौन्तेयो याहि याहीत्यचोदयत् ।\nभीष्मं प्रति महाराज जह्येनमिति चाब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Kunti urged Shikhandi, \"Go, go toward Bhishma, great king, and kill him!\""}},{"n":59,"text":"प्राग्ज्योतिषस्ततो हित्वा पाण्डवं पाण्डुपूर्वज ।\nप्रययौ त्वरितो राजन्द्रुपदस्य रथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhagadatta, O elder brother of Pandu's line, leaving the Pandava, rushed swiftly toward the chariot of Drupada's son."}},{"n":60,"text":"ततोऽर्जुनो महाराज भीष्ममभ्यद्रवद्द्रुतम् ।\nशिखण्डिनं पुरस्कृत्य ततो युद्धमवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Arjuna, great king, ran swiftly at Bhishma, with Shikhandi in front, and the fighting went on."}},{"n":61,"text":"ततस्ते तावकाः शूराः पाण्डवं रभसं रणे ।\nसर्वेऽभ्यधावन्क्रोशन्तस्तदद्भुतमिवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all your heroes ran shouting at the impetuous Pandava in the battle, and it was a marvel."}},{"n":62,"text":"नानाविधान्यनीकानि पुत्राणां ते जनाधिप ।\nअर्जुनो व्यधमत्काले दिवीवाभ्राणि मारुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord of men, Arjuna in that moment scattered the many divisions of your sons, as the wind scatters clouds in the sky."}},{"n":63,"text":"शिखण्डी तु समासाद्य भरतानां पितामहम् ।\nइषुभिस्तूर्णमव्यग्रो बहुभिः स समाचिनोत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shikhandi, reaching the grandsire of the Bharatas, calmly and quickly heaped many arrows on him."}},{"n":64,"text":"सोमकांश्च रणे भीष्मो जघ्ने पार्थपदानुगान् ।\nन्यवारयत सैन्यं च पाण्डवानां महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma killed the Somakas who followed in the footsteps of Arjuna, and the great warrior stopped the Pandava army."}},{"n":65,"text":"रथाग्न्यगारश्चापार्चिरसिशक्तिगदेन्धनः ।\nशरसंघमहाज्वालः क्षत्रियान्समरेऽदहत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With chariots as his hearth, bows as his flame, swords, spears and maces as his fuel, and volleys of arrows as his great blaze, he burned the kshatriyas in the battle."}},{"n":66,"text":"यथा हि सुमहानग्निः कक्षे चरति सानिलः ।\nतथा जज्वाल भीष्मोऽपि दिव्यान्यस्त्राण्युदीरयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a huge fire fanned by the wind rages through dry grass, so Bhishma blazed, calling forth divine weapons."}},{"n":67,"text":"सुवर्णपुङ्खैरिषुभिः शितैः संनतपर्वभिः ।\nनादयन्स दिशो भीष्मः प्रदिशश्च महायशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Filling every quarter and direction with the sound of gold-feathered, sharp, smooth-jointed arrows, the greatly renowned Bhishma"}},{"n":68,"text":"पातयन्रथिनो राजन्गजांश्च सह सादिभिः ।\nमुण्डतालवनानीव चकार स रथव्रजान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"brought down charioteers and elephants with their riders, king, and made the chariot-ranks like bare palm groves."}},{"n":69,"text":"निर्मनुष्यान्रथान्राजन्गजानश्वांश्च संयुगे ।\nचकार स तदा भीष्मः सर्वशस्त्रभृतां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma, best of all who bear weapons, then left chariots, elephants and horses in that battle empty of men."}},{"n":70,"text":"तस्य ज्यातलनिर्घोषं विस्फूर्जितमिवाशनेः ।\nनिशम्य सर्वतो राजन्समकम्पन्त सैनिकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the sound of his bowstring slapped on his palm, like thunder crashing, the soldiers on all sides trembled, king."}},{"n":71,"text":"अमोघा ह्यपतन्बाणाः पितुस्ते मनुजेश्वर ।\nनासज्जन्त शरीरेषु भीष्मचापच्युताः शराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your father's arrows, O lord of men, never missed their mark, and the arrows loosed from Bhishma's bow did not stay in the bodies they struck."}},{"n":72,"text":"निर्मनुष्यान्रथान्राजन्सुयुक्ताञ्जवनैर्हयैः ।\nवातायमानान्पश्याम ह्रियमाणान्विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"We saw chariots without men, well yoked to swift horses, being dragged along like the wind, O lord of the people."}},{"n":73,"text":"चेदिकाशिकरूषाणां सहस्राणि चतुर्दश ।\nमहारथाः समाख्याताः कुलपुत्रास्तनुत्यजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fourteen thousand great chariot-warriors of the Chedis, Kashis and Karushas, noble men of good families who had given up their lives,"}},{"n":74,"text":"अपरावर्तिनः शूराः सुवर्णविकृतध्वजाः ।\nसंग्रामे भीष्ममासाद्य सवाजिरथकुञ्जराः ।\nजग्मुस्ते परलोकाय व्यादितास्यमिवान्तकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"heroes who never turned back, with banners fashioned of gold, met Bhishma in battle with their horses, chariots and elephants, and went to the next world as into Death's open mouth."}},{"n":75,"text":"न तत्रासीन्महाराज सोमकानां महारथः ।\nयः संप्राप्य रणे भीष्मं जीविते स्म मनो दधे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Not one great warrior of the Somakas, great king, who came up against Bhishma in the fight, still held on to his life."}},{"n":76,"text":"तांश्च सर्वान्रणे योधान्प्रेतराजपुरं प्रति ।\nनीतानमन्यन्त जना दृष्ट्वा भीष्मस्य विक्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"People who saw Bhishma's prowess thought that all those warriors had been taken to the city of the king of the dead."}},{"n":77,"text":"न कश्चिदेनं समरे प्रत्युद्याति महारथः ।\nऋते पाण्डुसुतं वीरं श्वेताश्वं कृष्णसारथिम् ।\nशिखण्डिनं च समरे पाञ्चाल्यममितौजसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"No great warrior came out against him in the battle except the heroic son of Pandu, with white horses and Krishna as his charioteer, and Shikhandi, the Panchala of boundless energy."}},{"n":78,"text":"शिखण्डी तु रणे भीष्ममासाद्य भरतर्षभ ।\nदशभिर्दशभिर्बाणैराजघान महाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Shikhandi, reaching Bhishma in the great battle, O best of the Bharatas, struck him with ten arrows, ten again."}},{"n":79,"text":"शिखण्डिनं तु गाङ्गेयः क्रोधदीप्तेन चक्षुषा ।\nअवैक्षत कटाक्षेण निर्दहन्निव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Ganga looked at Shikhandi with eyes blazing with anger, sidelong, as though he would burn him, Bharata."}},{"n":80,"text":"स्त्रीत्वं तत्संस्मरन्राजन्सर्वलोकस्य पश्यतः ।\nन जघान रणे भीष्मः स च तं नावबुद्धवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yet remembering Shikhandi's womanhood, in sight of all the world Bhishma did not kill him in the battle, and Shikhandi did not understand why."}},{"n":81,"text":"अर्जुनस्तु महाराज शिखण्डिनमभाषत ।\nअभित्वरस्व त्वरितो जहि चैनं पितामहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Arjuna, great king, said to Shikhandi, \"Hurry, go quickly, and kill this grandsire!"}},{"n":82,"text":"किं ते विवक्षया वीर जहि भीष्मं महारथम् ।\nन ह्यन्यमनुपश्यामि कंचिद्यौधिष्ठिरे बले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Why do you hesitate to speak? Kill the great warrior Bhishma! I see no other in Yudhishthira's army"}},{"n":83,"text":"यः शक्तः समरे भीष्मं योधयेत पितामहम् ।\nऋते त्वां पुरुषव्याघ्र सत्यमेतद्ब्रवीमि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"who could fight the grandsire Bhishma in the battle, apart from you, tiger among men. I tell you this truly.\""}},{"n":84,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु पार्थेन शिखण्डी भरतर्षभ ।\nशरैर्नानाविधैस्तूर्णं पितामहमुपाद्रवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Spoken to so by the son of Pritha, O best of the Bharatas, Shikhandi quickly rushed at the grandsire with arrows of many kinds."}},{"n":85,"text":"अचिन्तयित्वा तान्बाणान्पिता देवव्रतस्तव ।\nअर्जुनं समरे क्रुद्धं वारयामास सायकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Paying no heed to those arrows, your father Devavrata held back the angry Arjuna in the battle with arrows."}},{"n":86,"text":"तथैव च चमूं सर्वां पाण्डवानां महारथः ।\nअप्रैषीत्समरे तीक्ष्णैः परलोकाय मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the same way the great warrior sent the whole Pandava army to the next world with sharp arrows, sir."}},{"n":87,"text":"तथैव पाण्डवा राजन्सैन्येन महता वृताः ।\nभीष्मं प्रच्छादयामासुर्मेघा इव दिवाकरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise the Pandavas, king, surrounded by a great army, covered Bhishma as clouds cover the sun."}},{"n":88,"text":"स समन्तात्परिवृतो भारतो भरतर्षभ ।\nनिर्ददाह रणे शूरान्वनं वह्निरिव ज्वलन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surrounded on every side, that Bharata, best of the Bharatas, burned up the heroes in the battle, blazing like a fire in a forest."}},{"n":89,"text":"तत्राद्भुतमपश्याम तव पुत्रस्य पौरुषम् ।\nअयोधयत यत्पार्थं जुगोप च यतव्रतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There we saw a wonder, the manliness of your son: he fought the son of Pritha and also protected Bhishma of firm vows."}},{"n":90,"text":"कर्मणा तेन समरे तव पुत्रस्य धन्विनः ।\nदुःशासनस्य तुतुषुः सर्वे लोका महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By that deed in the battle your archer son Duhshasana earned the praise of all people."}},{"n":91,"text":"यदेकः समरे पार्थान्सानुगान्समयोधयत् ।\nन चैनं पाण्डवा युद्धे वारयामासुरुल्बणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because he alone fought the sons of Pritha and their followers, the Pandavas could not stop him in the battle as he raged."}},{"n":92,"text":"दुःशासनेन समरे रथिनो विरथीकृताः ।\nसादिनश्च महाराज दन्तिनश्च महाबलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duhshasana made charioteers lose their chariots in the fight, and horsemen, great king, and mighty elephants."}},{"n":93,"text":"विनिर्भिन्नाः शरैस्तीक्ष्णैर्निपेतुर्धरणीतले ।\nशरातुरास्तथैवान्ये दन्तिनो विद्रुता दिशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Torn by his sharp arrows, they fell to the ground, and other elephants, pained by the arrows, fled in all directions."}},{"n":94,"text":"यथाग्निरिन्धनं प्राप्य ज्वलेद्दीप्तार्चिरुल्बणः ।\nतथा जज्वाल पुत्रस्ते पाण्डवान्वै विनिर्दहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a fire blazes up fierce with bright flames when it reaches fuel, so your son blazed, burning the Pandavas."}},{"n":95,"text":"तं भारतमहामात्रं पाण्डवानां महारथः ।\nजेतुं नोत्सहते कश्चिन्नाप्युद्यातुं कथंचन ।\nऋते महेन्द्रतनयं श्वेताश्वं कृष्णसारथिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"No great warrior of the Pandavas could defeat him, that chief supporter of the Bharatas, or even advance against him, except the son of Mahendra, Arjuna, with white horses and Krishna as charioteer."}},{"n":96,"text":"स हि तं समरे राजन्विजित्य विजयोऽर्जुनः ।\nभीष्ममेवाभिदुद्राव सर्वसैन्यस्य पश्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Victorious Arjuna, king, defeated him in the battle and then charged at Bhishma himself, in view of the whole army."}},{"n":97,"text":"विजितस्तव पुत्रोऽपि भीष्मबाहुव्यपाश्रयः ।\nपुनः पुनः समाश्वस्य प्रायुध्यत रणोत्कटः ।\nअर्जुनं च रणे राजन्योधयन्स व्यराजत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your son, defeated, relying on Bhishma's arms, took heart again and again and fought fiercely, and shone in the battle as he fought Arjuna, king."}},{"n":98,"text":"शिखण्डी तु रणे राजन्विव्याधैव पितामहम् ।\nशरैरशनिसंस्पर्शैस्तथा सर्पविषोपमैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Shikhandi, king, kept on wounding the grandsire with arrows that struck like thunderbolts and were like serpent venom."}},{"n":99,"text":"न च तेऽस्य रुजं चक्रुः पितुस्तव जनेश्वर ।\nस्मयमानश्च गाङ्गेयस्तान्बाणाञ्जगृहे तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those arrows did not hurt your father, lord of men; smiling, the son of Ganga received them."}},{"n":100,"text":"उष्णार्तो हि नरो यद्वज्जलधाराः प्रतीच्छति ।\nतथा जग्राह गाङ्गेयः शरधाराः शिखण्डिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a man tormented by heat welcomes streams of water, so the son of Ganga received Shikhandi's streams of arrows."}},{"n":101,"text":"तं क्षत्रिया महाराज ददृशुर्घोरमाहवे ।\nभीष्मं दहन्तं सैन्यानि पाण्डवानां महात्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The kshatriyas saw him, fearsome in the battle, burning the armies of the high-souled Pandavas."}},{"n":102,"text":"ततोऽब्रवीत्तव सुतः सर्वसैन्यानि मारिष ।\nअभिद्रवत संग्रामे फल्गुनं सर्वतो रथैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then your son, respected sir, said to all the troops, \"Charge at Phalguna from every side with your chariots!"}},{"n":103,"text":"भीष्मो वः समरे सर्वान्पालयिष्यति धर्मवित् ।\nते भयं सुमहत्त्यक्त्वा पाण्डवान्प्रतियुध्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma, who knows dharma, will protect you all in the battle. Put aside your great fear and fight the Pandavas."}},{"n":104,"text":"एष तालेन दीप्तेन भीष्मस्तिष्ठति पालयन् ।\nसर्वेषां धार्तराष्ट्राणां रणे शर्म च वर्म च ॥","meaning":{"en":"There stands Bhishma, whose palm-tree banner blazes, guarding all the sons of Dhritarashtra as their shield and shelter in the war."}},{"n":105,"text":"त्रिदशापि समुद्युक्ता नालं भीष्मं समासितुम् ।\nकिमु पार्था महात्मानं मर्त्यभूतास्तथाबलाः ।\nतस्माद्द्रवत हे योधाः फल्गुनं प्राप्य संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even the gods, if they strove, could not stand against Bhishma. How then could the sons of Pritha, who are mortal and weak in strength? So, warriors, run and meet Phalguna in the fight."}},{"n":106,"text":"अहमद्य रणे यत्तो योधयिष्यामि फल्गुनम् ।\nसहितः सर्वतो यत्तैर्भवद्भिर्वसुधाधिपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today I myself will take care to fight Phalguna, joined on all sides by you, rulers of the earth, as you stay vigilant.\""}},{"n":107,"text":"तच्छ्रुत्वा तु वचो राजंस्तव पुत्रस्य धन्विनः ।\nअर्जुनं प्रति संयत्ता बलवन्तो महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the words of your archer son, king, the powerful great warriors prepared against Arjuna."}},{"n":108,"text":"ते विदेहाः कलिङ्गाश्च दाशेरकगणैः सह ।\nअभिपेतुर्निषादाश्च सौवीराश्च महारणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Videhas, Kalingas and the Dasherakas, with the Nishadas and Sauviras, rushed forward in the great battle."}},{"n":109,"text":"बाह्लिका दरदाश्चैव प्राच्योदीच्याश्च मालवाः ।\nअभीषाहाः शूरसेनाः शिबयोऽथ वसातयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Bahlikas, Daradas, the people of the east and north, the Malavas, Abhishahas, Shurasenas, Shibis and Vasatis,"}},{"n":110,"text":"शाल्वाश्रयास्त्रिगर्ताश्च अम्बष्ठाः केकयैः सह ।\nअभिपेतू रणे पार्थं पतंगा इव पावकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"the Shalvas' allies, Trigartas and Ambashthas, with the Kekayas, fell on the son of Pritha like moths into a flame."}},{"n":111,"text":"स तान्सर्वान्सहानीकान्महाराज महारथान् ।\nदिव्यान्यस्त्राणि संचिन्त्य प्रसंधाय धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, Dhananjaya, thinking of his divine weapons and fitting them to the string, aimed at all those great warriors with their forces."}},{"n":112,"text":"स तैरस्त्रैर्महावेगैर्ददाहाशु महाबलः ।\nशरप्रतापैर्बीभत्सुः पतंगानिव पावकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With those swift and mighty weapons, powerful Bibhatsu quickly burned them with the heat of his arrows, as fire burns moths."}},{"n":113,"text":"तस्य बाणसहस्राणि सृजतो दृढधन्विनः ।\nदीप्यमानमिवाकाशे गाण्डीवं समदृश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that firm bowman released thousands of arrows, Gandiva seemed to blaze in the sky."}},{"n":114,"text":"ते शरार्ता महाराज विप्रकीर्णरथध्वजाः ।\nनाभ्यवर्तन्त राजानः सहिता वानरध्वजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tormented by the arrows, those kings, great king, with chariots and banners scattered, could not hold their ground together against the ape-bannered Arjuna."}},{"n":115,"text":"सध्वजा रथिनः पेतुर्हयारोहा हयैः सह ।\nगजाः सह गजारोहैः किरीटिशरताडिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chariot-fighters fell with their banners, riders with their horses, and elephants with their drivers, all struck by the arrows of the diadem-wearer."}},{"n":116,"text":"ततोऽर्जुनभुजोत्सृष्टैरावृतासीद्वसुंधरा ।\nविद्रवद्भिश्च बहुधा बलै राज्ञां समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth was covered with the arrows loosed from Arjuna's arms, and the kings' armies fled in many directions all around."}},{"n":117,"text":"अथ पार्थो महाबाहुर्द्रावयित्वा वरूथिनीम् ।\nदुःशासनाय समरे प्रेषयामास सायकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then mighty-armed Arjuna, having routed that army, sent arrows toward Duhshasana in the battle."}},{"n":118,"text":"ते तु भित्त्वा तव सुतं दुःशासनमयोमुखाः ।\nधरणीं विविशुः सर्वे वल्मीकमिव पन्नगाः ।\nहयांश्चास्य ततो जघ्ने सारथिं च न्यपातयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those iron-tipped arrows pierced your son Duhshasana and went into the earth, as snakes enter an anthill; then he killed his horses and felled his charioteer."}},{"n":119,"text":"विविंशतिं च विंशत्या विरथं कृतवान्प्रभो ।\nआजघान भृशं चैव पञ्चभिर्नतपर्वभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He left Vivimshati without a chariot with twenty arrows, my lord, and wounded him badly with five smooth-jointed ones."}},{"n":120,"text":"कृपं शल्यं विकर्णं च विद्ध्वा बहुभिरायसैः ।\nचकार विरथांश्चैव कौन्तेयः श्वेतवाहनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Kunti with white horses wounded Kripa, Shalya and Vikarna with many iron arrows and made them chariotless too."}},{"n":121,"text":"एवं ते विरथाः पञ्च कृपः शल्यश्च मारिष ।\nदुःशासनो विकर्णश्च तथैव च विविंशतिः ।\nसंप्राद्रवन्त समरे निर्जिताः सव्यसाचिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus the five, Kripa, Shalya, Duhshasana, Vikarna and Vivimshati, deprived of their chariots and defeated by Savyasachi, fled from the battle."}},{"n":122,"text":"पूर्वाह्णे तु तथा राजन्पराजित्य महारथान् ।\nप्रजज्वाल रणे पार्थो विधूम इव पावकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having defeated those great warriors in the forenoon, king, Arjuna blazed in the battle like a smokeless fire."}},{"n":123,"text":"तथैव शरवर्षेण भास्करो रश्मिवानिव ।\nअन्यानपि महाराज पातयामास पार्थिवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like the sun with its rays, he brought down other kings too, great king, with his showers of arrows."}},{"n":124,"text":"पराङ्मुखीकृत्य तदा शरवर्षैर्महारथान् ।\nप्रावर्तयत संग्रामे शोणितोदां महानदीम् ।\nमध्येन कुरुसैन्यानां पाण्डवानां च भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having turned those great warriors back with his arrow-showers, he made a great river of blood flow in the battle between the Kuru and the Pandava armies, Bharata."}},{"n":125,"text":"गजाश्च रथसंघाश्च बहुधा रथिभिर्हताः ।\nरथाश्च निहता नागैर्नागा हयपदातिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Elephants were slain by chariot-fighters in many ways, chariots by elephants, and elephants by horsemen and foot soldiers."}},{"n":126,"text":"अन्तरा छिध्यमानानि शरीराणि शिरांसि च ।\nनिपेतुर्दिक्षु सर्वासु गजाश्वरथयोधिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bodies and heads, cut through in the middle, fell in every direction from the fighters on elephants, horses and chariots."}},{"n":127,"text":"छन्नमायोधनं रेजे कुण्डलाङ्गदधारिभिः ।\nपतितैः पात्यमानैश्च राजपुत्रैर्महारथैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The battlefield, strewn with princes and great warriors wearing earrings and armlets, fallen or being felled, shone terribly."}},{"n":128,"text":"रथनेमिनिकृत्ताश्च गजैश्चैवावपोथिताः ।\nपादाताश्चाप्यदृश्यन्त साश्वाः सहयसादिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"We saw foot soldiers cut down by chariot rims and trampled by elephants, with horses and horsemen too."}},{"n":129,"text":"गजाश्वरथसंघाश्च परिपेतुः समन्ततः ।\nविशीर्णाश्च रथा भूमौ भग्नचक्रयुगध्वजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Masses of elephants, horses and chariots lay everywhere, and chariots with broken wheels, yokes and banners lay shattered on the ground."}},{"n":130,"text":"तद्गजाश्वरथौघानां रुधिरेण समुक्षितम् ।\nछन्नमायोधनं रेजे रक्ताभ्रमिव शारदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drenched in the blood of heaps of elephants, horses and chariots, the battlefield looked like an autumn sky red with clouds."}},{"n":131,"text":"श्वानः काकाश्च गृध्राश्च वृका गोमायुभिः सह ।\nप्रणेदुर्भक्ष्यमासाद्य विकृताश्च मृगद्विजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dogs, crows, vultures and wolves with jackals howled as they came upon their food, and deformed beasts and birds cried out."}},{"n":132,"text":"ववुर्बहुविधाश्चैव दिक्षु सर्वासु मारुताः ।\nदृश्यमानेषु रक्षःसु भूतेषु विनदत्सु च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Winds of many kinds blew in every direction, while demons were seen and spirits shrieked."}},{"n":133,"text":"काञ्चनानि च दामानि पताकाश्च महाधनाः ।\nधूमायमाना दृश्यन्ते सहसा मारुतेरिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Golden garlands and costly banners were seen suddenly smoking, stirred by the wind."}},{"n":134,"text":"श्वेतच्छत्रसहस्राणि सध्वजाश्च महारथाः ।\nविनिकीर्णाः स्म दृश्यन्ते शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ।\nसपताकाश्च मातङ्गा दिशो जग्मुः शरातुराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thousands of white umbrellas and great warriors with their banners were seen strewn about by hundreds and thousands, and elephants with pennants ran in all directions, pained by arrows."}},{"n":135,"text":"क्षत्रियाश्च मनुष्येन्द्र गदाशक्तिधनुर्धराः ।\nसमन्ततो व्यदृश्यन्त पतिता धरणीतले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kshatriyas who bore maces, spears and bows, king of men, were seen fallen on the ground all around."}},{"n":136,"text":"ततो भीष्मो महाराज दिव्यमस्त्रमुदीरयन् ।\nअभ्यधावत कौन्तेयं मिषतां सर्वधन्विनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhishma, great king, calling forth a divine weapon, rushed at the son of Kunti before the eyes of all the archers."}},{"n":137,"text":"तं शिखण्डी रणे यत्तमभ्यधावत दंशितः ।\nसंजहार ततो भीष्मस्तदस्त्रं पावकोपमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shikhandi, armored, ran at him as he strove in the battle, and then Bhishma withdrew that weapon which was like fire."}},{"n":138,"text":"एतस्मिन्नेव काले तु कौन्तेयः श्वेतवाहनः ।\nनिजघ्ने तावकं सैन्यं मोहयित्वा पितामहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"At that very time the son of Kunti with white horses, having bewildered the grandsire, cut down your army."}}]}]}